# Goal 6: Fix acosh (double) — wrong value

## Function
`acosh` (double-precision inverse hyperbolic cosine)

## Source files
- C: /home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/libm/mathd/acoshd.c
- Rust: /home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/newexp/rust-s3/src/mathd.rs

## Problem
acosh(2) = 0x1.62e42fefa39efp+0 (Rust) vs 0x1.5124271980434p+0 (C)

Rust returns ln(2) ≈ 0.6931 instead of arccosh(2) ≈ 1.3169. This suggests the Rust implementation may be using `log(x)` instead of the correct formula `log(x + sqrt(x*x - 1))`, or there's an error in the branch for x near 1 vs x > 2.

## What needs to change
Compare Rust acosh against C acoshd.c. Check the formula used — the C library likely uses `acosh(x) = log(2*x - 1/(x+sqrt(x*x-1)))` or similar for different ranges.

## Success Criteria
- `acosh 0x1p+1` = `0x1.5124271980434p+0` (bitwise exact)
- All other acosh tests continue to pass
